    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 A baseline report on the current national MPI dimensions and indicators including gaps and recommendation for improvement
1.2 Number of government entities engaged in the review of national MPI
1.3 Number of vulnerable communities engaged in the review of national MPI disaggregated by gender, age and disabilities 1.4 Number of vulnerable communities participated in the pilot study to test and validate national MPI questionnaire disaggregated by age, gender,  disabilities
1.5  A technical report on the robustness tests and candidate measures analysis including recommendation of final structure of national MPI
1.6 An operational guideline on how the measure MPI, monitor progress and report

2.1 Number of government officials including district officer trained on how to use disaggregated NMPI data for poverty targeting, coordination and monitoring
2.2 Number of government officials including district officers sensitized on gender mainstreaming on poverty and inequality measurement 
2.3 Number of members of parliament and government officialstrained on the MPI indicators and utilisation of MPI in policymaking for effective poverty alleviations initiatives 
2.4 Number of ministries and agencies in social protection consulted, reviewed and provided with a technical advisory and/or implementation guide for specific development challenges ie to coordinate, finetune their interventions

3.1 A Communication Strategy and Plan with an appropriate timeline and resources
3.2 Number of communication and advocacy materials published for different target groups  
3.3 Number of communication events to promote MPI utilisation for evidence-based  decision making at the federal and local level
3.4 A detailed documentation of Malaysia MPI journey</narrative>
